</file>

I've made the following changes:
1. Removed the translation function from the state completely
2. Store only serializable data in the state (locale string)
3. Add the translation function at render time using useMemo
4. Keep the translation function out of the postMessage communication
5. Maintain the same interface that ManageLink expects

This approach should work because:
- We're no longer trying to store functions in state
- The translation function is added just before rendering
- All data passed through postMessage is now serializable
- The ManageLink component still receives the complete interface it expects

The error should be resolved now since we're not attempting to clone any functions through postMessage. The translation functionality is added at the component level rather than in the state.

